 ## Background
-The Mesh Winding Number was introduced by Alec Jacobson, Ladislav Kavan, and Olga Sorkine-Hornung in a SIGGRAPH paper in 2013 [S1, unofficial]. It extends the concept of the 2D polygon winding number to 3D meshes, providing a robust way to determine point containment. The hierarchical implementation leverages bounding volume hierarchies to accelerate the computation for large-scale voxelization tasks [S1, unofficial].
